---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Related from "../components/Related.astro";
import { VatCalc } from "../components/Calculators.jsx";
import { toolSchema, todaySA } from "../lib/site.js";

const faqs = [
  ["What is the VAT rate in South Africa?", "The standard VAT rate is 15%. Some items, such as certain basic foods and exports, are zero-rated, and some services are exempt."],
  ["How do I remove VAT from a price?", "Divide the VAT-inclusive price by 1.15. To get only the VAT amount, multiply the inclusive price by 15/115."],
  ["When must a business register for VAT?", "Registration becomes compulsory once taxable turnover passes the SARS threshold in a 12-month period. Check the current threshold on the SARS website before deciding."],
];
---
<Base title="VAT Calculator South Africa (15%) – Add or Remove VAT Instantly (2026)"
  description="Free 15% VAT calculator for South Africa. Add VAT to a price or remove VAT from an inclusive amount instantly, with the formulas explained."
  h1="VAT calculator (15%)" lede="Add or remove South African VAT from any amount."
  trail={[["Home", "/"], ["VAT calculator", "/vat-calculator/"]]} faqs={faqs} updated={todaySA()}
  schema={toolSchema("VAT Calculator", "/vat-calculator/", "Add or remove 15% South African VAT.")}>
  <VatCalc client:load />
  <h2>How to calculate VAT in South Africa</h2>
  <p>The standard VAT rate in South Africa is 15%.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Add VAT:</strong> multiply the VAT-exclusive price by 1.15. R1 000 × 1.15 = R1 150.</li>
    <li><strong>Remove VAT:</strong> divide the VAT-inclusive price by 1.15. R1 150 ÷ 1.15 = R1 000.</li>
    <li><strong>VAT portion of an inclusive price:</strong> multiply by 15 and divide by 115.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <div class="example"><p>A supplier quotes <strong>R4 350 excluding VAT</strong>. VAT is R4 350 × 0.15 = R652.50, so you'll pay <strong>R5 002.50</strong>. If a till slip shows <strong>R2 300 including VAT</strong>, the price before VAT is R2 300 ÷ 1.15 = R2 000 and the VAT is R300.</p></div>
  <p>A common mistake is subtracting 15% from an inclusive price. That gives R977.50 instead of R1 000, because the 15% was added to the smaller, exclusive amount.</p>
  <Related exclude="vat-calculator" answersFor="vat-calculator" />
</Base>
